WEBVTT

1
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.191
<i>Once upon a Christmas Eve...</i>

2
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.035
<i>... the</i> Nutcracker <i>ballet was performed</i>
<i>to everyone's delight.</i>

3
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.760
<i>And while this ballet</i>
<i>had many admirers...</i>

4
00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:42.153
<i>... in this theater, it had no greater fan</i>
<i>than little Jerry Mouse.</i>

5
00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.749
<i>Meanwhile, outside the theater...</i>

6
00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.518
<i>King of the cats</i>
<i>That's what he is</i>

7
00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:06.829
<i>Takin ' all our sustenance</i>

8
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.479
<i>Like it was really his</i>

9
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:09.993
<i>Greedy to a fault</i>

10
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.309
<i>Bully to us all</i>

11
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:14.358
<i>He'll only be your friend</i>
<i>So you can take the fall</i>

12
00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:17.318
<i>But he's really something special</i>

13
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.278
<i>Something you just can 't deny</i>

14
00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:22.874
<i>Everybody raise a cheer</i>

15
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.873
<i>Mainly 'cause we know he's here</i>

16
00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.792
<i>Everybody raise a cheer</i>

17
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.748
<i>To the king of the cats</i>

18
00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.793
<i>King of the cats</i>

19
00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.552
<i>That's what I am</i>

20
00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:38.109
<i>Pushing 'em around</i>
<i>Because I know I can</i>

21
00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.599
<i>Greedy to a fault</i>

22
00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:40.909
<i>Bully to 'em all</i>

23
00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.629
<i>- He'll only be your friend</i>
<i>- So you can take the fall</i>

24
00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.993
<i>But he's really something special</i>

25
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.799
<i>Something you just can 't deny</i>

26
00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.428
<i>Everybody raise a cheer</i>

27
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.239
<i>Mainly 'cause we know he's here</i>

28
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:00.477
<i>Everybody raise a cheer</i>

29
00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:04.553
<i>To the king of the cats</i>

30
00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.271
<i>Now he must sadly wait...</i>

31
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.876
<i>... another long year</i>
<i>until the next performance.</i>

32
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:16.918
<i>Nothing for Jerry in this empty place...</i>

33
00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.469
<i>... except his love of the ballet.</i>

34
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.278
<i>If only he could dance.</i>

35
00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.792
<i>What's the use of pretending?</i>

36
00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.199
<i>These things never change.</i>

37
00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.193
<i>Why, that would take a miracle.</i>

38
00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.160
Bravo! Bravo!

39
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.278
<i>But wait! A mouse needs more.</i>

40
00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:36.833
<i>And a mouse king needs his royal court.</i>

41
00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.076
No worries. You can't hurt a quality toy.

42
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.549
<i>And a ballet needs a ballerina.</i>

43
00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.398
A lovely couple, no? Sorry.

44
00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:48.075
<i>Come to think of it,</i>
<i>a mouse king needs a kingdom too.</i>

45
00:04:48.440 --> 00:04:50.510
<i>Even if it's built on fragile magic.</i>

46
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.912
<i>But of course,</i>
<i>magic affects both friend and foe alike.</i>

47
00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.272
Boys, round up them worthless toys.

48
00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:49.159
I'm taking over this kingdom.

49
00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.720
Oh, Jerry, what shall we do?

50
00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.713
Cease and desist, pussycat.

51
00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.510
This is Monsieur Jerry's wish.

52
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:36.318
All he wanted was to dance.

53
00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:39.392
And this kingdom
sprang from those desires.

54
00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:43.112
We must respect his dream, no?

55
00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.319
Oh, Mr. Cat, I have a present for you.

56
00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.152
Me?

57
00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.273
Thanks. It's what I've always wanted.

58
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:15.794
Isn't that a bomb?

59
00:07:15.960 --> 00:07:17.109
A bomb?!

60
00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:20.798
Somebody, do something.

61
00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:28.434
Slacker. Stop those toys.

62
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:29.749
Get moving!

63
00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:24.072
Whoa, Nelly!

64
00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:47.428
Prime Minister Lackey!

65
00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.431
So, what's the state of my kingdom?

66
00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.273
I have some grave misgivings
about the treatment of the toys.

67
00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.873
Enough. You're bringing me down.

68
00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.156
So where's that little dancing doll?

69
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:58.477
Prepare to be amused.

70
00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:01.071
Oh, goody. Take a hike, Tim.

71
00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.878
Now, how about a little dance?

72
00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:06.634
Oh, I get it. You need music.

73
00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:11.754
Not a big fan of the banjo, huh?

74
00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.510
I will never dance for you.
You've ruined everything.

75
00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.069
Everybody seems pretty happy
around here to me.

76
00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:23.997
It doesn't matter. There's nothing
you or anybody can do about it.

77
00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.434
You forget about Jerry.

78
00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:29.431
Your little mouse king? That's a riot.

79
00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.398
Don't underestimate him.
He will never give up.

80
00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.148
You can't give up yet.

81
00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.390
Why, alls we need is a great idea.

82
00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.113
Sorry, I can only talk
if someone gives my string a pull.

83
00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:50.795
I was thinking,
we need someone to aid us.

84
00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.917
And?

85
00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.237
And I have this tag
that reads "The Toymaker."

86
00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:02.994
Well, I got one too. Kind of itches.

87
00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.549
So you think
we should find the Toymaker?

88
00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:07.312
If he even exists.

89
00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:08.629
Of course he does.

90
00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:11.633
Somebody made us
and his name is Toymaker.

91
00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:13.791
Yes, but where can we find him?

92
00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:17.873
Well, maybe you can
contribute something here.

93
00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:24.949
Follow the star?

94
00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.953
I guess that's worked before.

95
00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.753
You know, I've been thinking...

96
00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:33.275
...maybe it wouldn't hurt
to finish off that mouse.

97
00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.158
Just to be on the safe side.

98
00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:36.958
So whom should we send?

99
00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:39.475
- How about Tim?
- I think you mean Tom.

100
00:10:39.640 --> 00:10:41.232
Very well, Tim it is.

101
00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.719
Tom, sir.

102
00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.276
Tim, take all the men you need
and make sure...

103
00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:46.953
...that mouse never comes back.

104
00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:48.633
Get it?

105
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:59.117
<i>So, by the command of the cat king...</i>

106
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:04.071
<i>... Tom gathered his troops</i>
<i>and set off to catch a mouse.</i>

107
00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:05.355
<i>We're marching off to fight</i>

108
00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:07.317
<i>We'll catch that mouse</i>
<i>And do what's right</i>

109
00:11:07.480 --> 00:11:10.631
<i>We're marching off to fight</i>
<i>To go and get that mouse</i>

110
00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.758
<i>Hey, ho, away we go</i>
<i>One, two, three, in a row</i>

111
00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.832
<i>We're marching round and round</i>
<i>To go and crush that mouse.</i>

112
00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.911
<i>We're heading off to fight</i>
<i>We'll march and march</i>

113
00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.069
<i>All through the night</i>

114
00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:23.312
<i>We're heading off to fight</i>
<i>To go and beat that mouse</i>

115
00:11:23.480 --> 00:11:26.517
<i>Hey, ho, off we go</i>
<i>Hit him high and hit him low</i>

116
00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:29.911
<i>We're heading off to fight</i>
<i>To go and mince that mouse.</i>

117
00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.677
<i>We're marching off to fight</i>
<i>We'll fight our foe with all our might</i>

118
00:11:45.840 --> 00:11:48.957
<i>We're marching off to fight</i>
<i>To go and break that mouse</i>

119
00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:52.157
<i>Hey, ho, away we go</i>
<i>Loaded down with guns in tow</i>

120
00:11:52.320 --> 00:11:56.393
<i>We're marching off to fight</i>
<i>To go and squash that mouse</i>

121
00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.636
Maybe we should send the chicken.

122
00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:39.272
Mademoiselle Ballerina Lady!

123
00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.192
I am coming to rescue you.

124
00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.271
- Tuffy?
- Yes, it is I.

125
00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.953
And I will set you free.

126
00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.680
Oh, Tuffy, the cats are heading out
to destroy Jerry.

127
00:12:47.840 --> 00:12:50.479
Time is of the essence.
You must warn him.

128
00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.790
Then take these keys and free yourself.

129
00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.673
Hurry, Tuffy. Hurry!

130
00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:58.070
I shall not fail you.

131
00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:47.313
<i>Hold it. What's this?</i>

132
00:13:55.040 --> 00:13:58.237
<i>Looks like Tom is carving a path</i>
<i>straight to Jerry.</i>

133
00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:01.233
<i>That little mouse is gonna need</i>
<i>all the luck he can get.</i>

134
00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.755
Are you sure this is it?

135
00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.759
A toy wouldn't head through
that scary place.

136
00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:48.912
A river.

137
00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.795
All right, I've got a confession to make.

138
00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:54.188
I'm not really a toy.

139
00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.636
I'm only a decoration, an ornament,
not suitable for play.

140
00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.439
If I get wet, I'm liable
to start falling apart.

141
00:15:11.880 --> 00:15:13.552
Well, it is frozen solid.

142
00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.988
Hey. Looks like fun...

143
00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.798
I got it. Thanks.

144
00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:36.591
Hey, look at me.

145
00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:39.152
I'm skating.

146
00:16:14.800 --> 00:16:16.472
Oh, no. I think he's stuck.

147
00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:23.992
Come on, Jer, you can do it.

148
00:16:25.440 --> 00:16:27.510
No. Don't give up, buddy.

149
00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.195
Please, we need you.

150
00:16:47.960 --> 00:16:49.871
Help me, Nelly.

151
00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.957
Oh, boy.
You scared the stuffings out of us.

152
00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:57.874
We gotta get you someplace warm.

153
00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:05.391
Hey, little lady, what's going on here?

154
00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:09.759
A string attached to keys...

155
00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:12.150
...can only mean one thing:

156
00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:14.311
Playtime.

157
00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:17.278
Your majesty, I have some...
What is going on here?

158
00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:19.749
Me and the little ballerina
are playing keys.

159
00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:23.150
You should really try it sometime.

160
00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:25.629
Yes, it sounds fascinating.

161
00:17:25.800 --> 00:17:27.279
I know what you're trying to do.

162
00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.874
You're attempting
to distract the king from his duties.

163
00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:34.272
Well, it won't work.
Here, I haven't got all day.

164
00:17:34.800 --> 00:17:37.109
She's got more keys than I do.

165
00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:41.669
Clever. But we'll have
no more of this nonsense.

166
00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:44.593
I hope I make myself clear.

167
00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:58.237
Send up the telescope.

168
00:17:58.400 --> 00:18:00.231
- The telescope.
- The telescope.

169
00:18:00.400 --> 00:18:02.311
The telescope.

170
00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:18.710
Do not harm Monsieur Jerry.
Be kind and gentle.

171
00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:20.518
This is your conscience speaking.

172
00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:24.468
The little voice
that tells you right from wrong.

173
00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:28.030
The quality of mercy is not strained.

174
00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:31.199
It dropeth as a gentle rain from heaven.

175
00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.158
Look, there he is.

176
00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:43.759
Why do you listen to that little fool?
I say do the mouse in.

177
00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.197
No. I appeal to your better nature.

178
00:18:47.360 --> 00:18:50.033
Do not listen to this ruffian.

179
00:18:50.200 --> 00:18:52.395
Well, at least I'm not wearing a dress.

180
00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:54.835
Time to rub out the rodent.

181
00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.037
Please, I beseech you to...

182
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:00.513
Well, think it over.

183
00:19:01.480 --> 00:19:03.550
Sleep on it, won't you?

184
00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:08.754
Sometimes a conscience
must take drastic measures.

185
00:19:21.000 --> 00:19:22.991
Feeling better, Jerry?

186
00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:25.872
I'm coming undone. I knew it.

187
00:19:26.040 --> 00:19:27.951
The water must have melted my glue.

188
00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:31.715
Oh, we have to put a stop to that.
I had an aunt who started to unravel.

189
00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.393
Not a pretty picture, huh?

190
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:39.468
What? Oh, of course, the Toymaker.

191
00:19:39.640 --> 00:19:41.153
He'll be able to fix you right up.

192
00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:42.514
Sure, no worries.

193
00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.790
<i>Bonjour,</i> Monsieur Jerry. It is I.

194
00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:52.035
- What are you doing here, Tuffy?
- The ballerina lady sent me to warn you.

195
00:19:52.200 --> 00:19:53.553
Warn us about what?

196
00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.551
- The cats.
- The cats?

197
00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:57.392
They are coming to do away with you.

198
00:19:57.560 --> 00:20:00.597
They are probably surrounding us
even as we speak.

199
00:22:27.440 --> 00:22:29.749
That doesn't sound
much like a mouse to me.

200
00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:33.076
It's more of a... No, it sounds like...

201
00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:34.958
Oh, I can't put my finger on it.

202
00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:39.030
You know, that sounds like a cat.

203
00:22:39.200 --> 00:22:41.589
- You sure?
- Well, not a hundred percent.

204
00:22:43.280 --> 00:22:45.191
Oh, yeah, definitely a cat.

205
00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:56.076
That brings your batting average to.340

206
00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:02.431
There it is, Jerry, bright as day.

207
00:23:03.720 --> 00:23:06.837
The Toymaker must be
right over this ridge.

208
00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:11.716
Has Monsieur Paulie lost his head again?

209
00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:14.713
I'm not lost. I'm in here.

210
00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:37.195
You know,
I like you better without your head.

211
00:23:45.520 --> 00:23:47.431
So good of you to bridge the gap.

212
00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:20.399
There's nothing to fear.

213
00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:24.599
We just need to find Monsieur Paulie's
head and be on our way.

214
00:24:26.680 --> 00:24:29.433
Did I mention
that I prefer him without it?

215
00:25:08.520 --> 00:25:10.795
Hey, fellows. I'm over here.

216
00:28:20.840 --> 00:28:23.308
I see you managed to hang on
to one of those keys.

217
00:28:23.480 --> 00:28:25.198
But if you wanna make it work...

218
00:28:25.360 --> 00:28:27.271
...you gotta tie it to a string.

219
00:30:25.240 --> 00:30:27.674
Asleep, finally.

220
00:30:47.280 --> 00:30:51.353
Oh, Monsieur Jerry, how can we
ever reach the Toymaker from here?

221
00:31:00.400 --> 00:31:02.789
Do you have any idea
what we're celebrating?

222
00:31:11.000 --> 00:31:14.356
Don't worry. I'll hang on
to you like a fat man to a doughnut.

223
00:32:15.360 --> 00:32:16.952
Oh, boy.

224
00:32:20.520 --> 00:32:22.112
Careful, Tuffy.

225
00:32:25.080 --> 00:32:27.116
Whoa, Nelly!

226
00:32:38.280 --> 00:32:40.236
Talk about holding on by a thread.

227
00:32:40.600 --> 00:32:42.511
Tuffy, set her down someplace, quick.

228
00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:54.120
I told you I wouldn't let go.

229
00:33:39.800 --> 00:33:42.394
I can't. I'm just too scared.

230
00:33:49.880 --> 00:33:52.553
I guess I'm just not cut out
to save the day.

231
00:34:02.880 --> 00:34:04.711
We've gotta find out
where they're headed.

232
00:34:04.880 --> 00:34:06.711
But how are we gonna get her to talk?

233
00:34:07.960 --> 00:34:09.996
I think I can help you with that.

234
00:34:11.120 --> 00:34:13.190
Let me see the tongue-tied patient.

235
00:34:13.880 --> 00:34:16.553
I have special methods
for restoring speech.

236
00:34:23.840 --> 00:34:26.559
So tell me, my dear,
where are your friends headed?

237
00:34:29.560 --> 00:34:31.278
They're off to see the Toymaker.

238
00:34:31.640 --> 00:34:33.153
Did you hear? The Toymaker!

239
00:34:33.320 --> 00:34:36.710
Why, a guy like that's liable
to cause big trouble for us.

240
00:34:36.880 --> 00:34:40.475
And just how can we find this Toymaker?

241
00:34:42.040 --> 00:34:44.474
Follow the star. It will lead you to him.

242
00:34:49.880 --> 00:34:51.711
See? That didn't hurt a bit.

243
00:34:51.880 --> 00:34:53.233
At least not physically.

244
00:34:54.280 --> 00:34:55.633
She's a traitor now.

245
00:34:55.800 --> 00:34:59.395
She can't go back to her friends.
They'll hate her.

246
00:35:02.680 --> 00:35:04.432
And I thought I was cruel.

247
00:35:30.640 --> 00:35:32.870
I can't believe it. Finally.

248
00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:34.553
You were right, Monsieur Jerry.

249
00:35:34.720 --> 00:35:36.711
All we had to do was follow the star.

250
00:35:39.040 --> 00:35:40.234
A little help here.

251
00:35:47.840 --> 00:35:49.796
Can you imagine?
I got snagged on a branch.

252
00:35:49.960 --> 00:35:53.032
Sure hope the Toymaker's got
some knitting needles.

253
00:36:03.520 --> 00:36:04.873
We've done it.

254
00:36:06.320 --> 00:36:07.992
Nothing can stop us now.

255
00:36:10.240 --> 00:36:13.437
Sorry, boys,
but this is the end of the line.

256
00:36:13.600 --> 00:36:17.354
- How'd you know we were coming here?
- Your little horsey friend told us.

257
00:36:17.520 --> 00:36:21.991
I shall pummel you vigorously
if you hurt but a single hair in her mane.

258
00:36:22.160 --> 00:36:26.073
Hurt her? Alls we did was pull her string
and we couldn't shut her up.

259
00:36:26.240 --> 00:36:28.800
Monsieur Jerry, we have come so far.

260
00:36:28.960 --> 00:36:33.397
Monsieur Jerry, we have come so far.

261
00:36:40.160 --> 00:36:42.151
Are you fine fellows here to see me?

262
00:36:42.800 --> 00:36:45.268
We are, sir, if you are the Toymaker.

263
00:36:45.440 --> 00:36:47.112
At your service, lads.

264
00:36:47.280 --> 00:36:49.999
You're also a toy repairer right?

265
00:36:50.160 --> 00:36:53.835
Don't you worry.
I've fixed a toy or two in my time.

266
00:36:56.000 --> 00:36:58.560
I suppose I should tell you,
I'm not really a toy.

267
00:36:58.720 --> 00:37:01.439
Yes, I remember. You're a decoration.

268
00:37:01.600 --> 00:37:03.158
Not suitable for play.

269
00:37:03.320 --> 00:37:07.518
But you have the heart of a toy.
And so you shall be one, my son.

270
00:37:07.680 --> 00:37:11.116
Sir, we've come a great distance
to ask for your help.

271
00:37:11.280 --> 00:37:15.114
I know why you've come.
In fact, I know a lot about you.

272
00:37:15.520 --> 00:37:19.832
I've been following your adventures
for longer than you know.

273
00:37:22.320 --> 00:37:24.311
You need a solution to your cat problem.

274
00:37:25.840 --> 00:37:27.831
Well, I think I've got the answer.

275
00:37:28.000 --> 00:37:30.230
Do you know
what has become of our friend?

276
00:37:31.720 --> 00:37:32.994
Nelly?

277
00:37:33.160 --> 00:37:35.310
I'm afraid she's become discouraged.

278
00:37:35.480 --> 00:37:36.959
She feels she's betrayed you...

279
00:37:37.120 --> 00:37:39.350
...and that you'd never want
to see her again.

280
00:37:44.960 --> 00:37:46.712
I knew I was right about you.

281
00:37:46.880 --> 00:37:48.552
Little mice with big hearts.

282
00:37:48.720 --> 00:37:50.870
- Are you ready?
- Ready for what?

283
00:37:51.040 --> 00:37:54.828
Presenting the new
and improved Paulie Pixie.

284
00:37:55.000 --> 00:37:56.592
Thanks, T.M. Guess what.

285
00:37:56.760 --> 00:37:59.513
I'm a real toy.
Suitable for aggressive play patterns.

286
00:37:59.680 --> 00:38:02.558
- Oh, Paulie, may I?
- Be my guest.

287
00:38:02.720 --> 00:38:04.950
Go ahead, pull harder. Harder.

288
00:38:05.120 --> 00:38:07.839
It's okay.
I used a lot more glue this time.

289
00:38:08.000 --> 00:38:09.592
But there's something you must know.

290
00:38:09.760 --> 00:38:13.878
When the sun rises, the magic that
created your kingdom will begin to fade.

291
00:38:14.040 --> 00:38:15.837
And if you fail to reclaim your throne...

292
00:38:16.000 --> 00:38:18.230
...by the time the sun has climbed
into the sky...

293
00:38:18.400 --> 00:38:20.960
...it will remain
the domain of the cats forever.

294
00:38:21.120 --> 00:38:23.270
But there is a way
to recapture your kingdom.

295
00:38:23.440 --> 00:38:26.876
And this, my little friend, is the key.

296
00:38:29.120 --> 00:38:31.759
I wish I could stay
to see what's in store for you...

297
00:38:31.920 --> 00:38:35.276
...but I have some important errands
I must run.

298
00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:39.035
<i>Merci beaucoup,</i> Monsieur Toymaker,
for everything.

299
00:38:39.200 --> 00:38:43.637
What did he mean by "in store"
and what is that key do?

300
00:39:17.640 --> 00:39:19.153
Sir, what are you doing?

301
00:39:19.880 --> 00:39:21.393
Well...

302
00:39:21.560 --> 00:39:23.471
...certainly not playing with keys.

303
00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:25.358
Keys?

304
00:39:26.760 --> 00:39:27.954
Oh, dear.

305
00:39:28.120 --> 00:39:31.317
Don't worry. She left this.

306
00:39:31.480 --> 00:39:33.072
Guards! Guards!

307
00:39:33.240 --> 00:39:34.832
Find that ballerina!

308
00:39:58.600 --> 00:40:01.876
Do you mind?
We're right in the middle of a doll crisis.

309
00:40:13.360 --> 00:40:15.999
Oh, boy. Do something.

310
00:40:19.040 --> 00:40:21.838
Don't just stand there. Do something!

311
00:41:28.600 --> 00:41:33.310
Lower the drawbridge!
Lower the drawbridge!

312
00:41:34.560 --> 00:41:35.993
It seems we've found her.

313
00:41:36.160 --> 00:41:38.151
Toys, for freedom!

314
00:41:38.880 --> 00:41:40.711
Move it!

315
00:41:51.760 --> 00:41:53.751
Is this the end?

316
00:41:53.920 --> 00:41:55.990
Oh, it can't be. It can't be!

317
00:42:02.960 --> 00:42:04.393
Go, Nelly!

318
00:42:49.400 --> 00:42:50.992
Retreat!

319
00:43:33.560 --> 00:43:35.391
Oh, Jerry!

320
00:43:35.560 --> 00:43:37.152
I never doubted you.

321
00:43:46.880 --> 00:43:48.711
Is she...?

322
00:43:58.640 --> 00:44:00.790
She was the bravest one of us all.

323
00:44:20.760 --> 00:44:22.557
I'm alive.

324
00:44:22.720 --> 00:44:26.349
And I can talk. Without a string.

325
00:44:27.920 --> 00:44:29.194
Look at them.

326
00:44:29.360 --> 00:44:33.239
Now that's what I call a happy ending.

327
00:46:46.720 --> 00:46:48.711
Subtitles by
SDI Media Group

328
00:46:48.880 --> 00:46:50.871
[ENGLISH]
